From 0c0db005625ff5f3633f5c5530c394b88aaba191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:19:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(js): custom element reactions wrap only elements that
 can have a definition

Once any custom element was defined, every insert, removal and innerHTML
queried all elements of the subtree, wrapped each one in a JS object kept in
the node cache, and checked it for a definition and a shadow root. Only a
name with a hyphen can be defined, so a native shadow-including walk now
returns just those elements, in the same order. Five innerHTML writes of
15,000 elements with a defined element present: 401 ms before, 102 ms
after; appending the same subtree: 66 ms before, 5 ms after; the same 60
connectedCallback calls.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
